# ─── Your recordings and transcripts stay yours ──────────────────────────────
#
# This section exists for everyone who clones this repo, not just its author.
# Transcripts contain the full text of whatever you recorded, and job records
# additionally embed the absolute path of the source file. None of that should
# ever reach a remote by accident, so anywhere your own content could plausibly
# land inside a clone is ignored by default.
#
# If you genuinely want to commit a transcript, force it: `git add -f <path>`.

# Job records: job.json holds the source path plus every transcript segment.
data/

# Transcript outputs, wherever they land. The CLI writes these into a folder
# named after the media file, which ends up inside the repo whenever the source
# media does. review.md quotes the recording verbatim, same as the rest.
transcript.json
transcript.srt
transcript.txt
review.md

# Folders the CLI creates beside media files that live in the repo.
test-fixtures/*/
server/test/fixtures/media/*/

# Common places people drop their own material.
/recordings/
/input/
/output/
/transcripts/
/media/

# Media files anywhere, so dropping a recording into the repo to try it out
# can't turn into a commit. The project's own committed fixtures are
# re-included below.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.aiff
*.aif
*.caf

# …except these, which are small, generated by scripts/make-fixtures.sh from
# macOS's built-in `say`, and intentionally part of the repo.
!test-fixtures/speech-short.aiff
!test-fixtures/two-voice-interview.wav
!server/test/fixtures/media/basic.wav
!server/test/fixtures/media/basic2.wav

# Scenario selectors for the fake helper, which picks its behaviour from the
# input's basename and never opens the file — so these are 0-byte placeholders,
# not media. They must be committed or the unit suite fails on a fresh clone.
!server/test/fixtures/media/damaged-midfile.mp3
!server/test/fixtures/media/damaged-at-zero.mp3

# Credentials, in case anyone wires this into something that needs them.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Build output and tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────

.DS_Store
node_modules/
dist/
.build/

# ─── Fixtures deliberately not committed ─────────────────────────────────────

# Generated by scripts/make-fixtures.sh; not committed because it embeds most
# of a macOS system audio resource byte-for-byte (see the script's comments).
# Regenerate locally before running the E2E suite's MP3-repair case. The .json
# sidecar (true/declared duration) is generated alongside it and ignored for
# the same reason — it's meaningless without the fixture it describes.
test-fixtures/malformed.mp3
test-fixtures/malformed.mp3.json

# Third-party sample media: unclear redistribution terms, so it's fetched by
# scripts/make-fixtures.sh rather than committed.
test-fixtures/sample-5s.mp4

# Internal working notes (measurements, subagent reports) — not part of the
# project.
.superpowers/
